      "side": 1,
      "message": "Optional but highly recommended: To prevent bugs in the future, I suggest adding the following `static_assert`\u0027s to ensure `vin` and `vout` are large enough:\n\n```\n    SIMD_ALIGNED(TS vin[64 * 2]);                                              \\\n    static_assert((MASK + 1) * SBPP \u003c\u003d 64, \"\");                                \\\n    SIMD_ALIGNED(TD vout[64]);                                                 \\\n    static_assert((MASK + 1) * BPP \u003c\u003d 64, \"\");                                 \\\n```\n\nNote: `static_assert` is available in C11 (need to include \u003cassert.h\u003e). I recommend starting using `static_assert` to prevent this kind of buffer overflow in the future.",
